Tokyo Gâteau
Serves: 6
Prep: 15 min
Cook: 25 min
Total: 4 hr
Source: Dandelion Chocolate Japan
Equipment: Loaf tin 17×6×6 cm (500 ml), Baking paper, 2 bowls, Saucepan for a water bath, Whisk, Spatula, Tea strainer

Unmould: Lift out by the paper only once **completely firm**. Slice with a hot knife.
  Chill (3 hr+): Cool to room temperature, then into the fridge. It's soft when warm and **breaks if unmoulded early**.
    Bake (heat, 25 min): Into the oven, then turn it **down to 140 °C**. Turn the tin round after **20 min**.
      Fold (combine): Pour the chocolate into the eggs and mix **only until it comes together**: overmixing cools and splits it. Into the tin; tap out the air.
        Melt (heat): Oven to **150 °C**. Line the tin with paper. Melt the butter in a bowl over barely simmering water, **below 60 °C**. Add the chocolate and stir until smooth. Too hot and it scorches.
          - 75 g | Unsalted butter
          - 120 g | Dark chocolate | 70%, single-origin if possible
        Warm (heat): Beat the eggs and push them through a tea strainer. Add the sugar and stir over the water bath until it **dissolves**.
          - 2 | Eggs
          - 50 g | Light cane sugar | or 60 g caster sugar
